  "response": "## Finding\n\n`crime_00070` — **Duplicate Component Shape** (medium, confidence 0.7). The same 9-line `<div>` subtree — a form footer with a Cancel link + submit Button — appears in 4 invoice form files.\n\n## Files that share the shape\n\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx:142-150`\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx:152-160`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx:101-109`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx:112-120`\n\nThe repeated subtree:\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n  <Link href=\"/dashboard/invoices\" className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\">\n    Cancel\n  </Link>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">{Create|Edit} Invoice</Button>\n</div>\n```\n\nOnly two things actually vary across the four copies: the **Cancel `href`** (currently identical, but a real fix shouldn't bake it in) and the **submit button label** (`Create Invoice` vs `Edit Invoice`).\n\n## Proposed shared component\n\n`app/ui/form-actions.tsx` — co-locate with the other shared UI in `app/ui/`. Both example apps (`final-example`, `starter-example`) would import the same module; if those are independent deployables, hoist to a workspace package (`@dashboard/ui`) or keep one copy per app and let each import locally.\n\n```tsx\n// app/ui/form-actions.tsx\nimport Link from 'next/link';\nimport { Button } from '@/app/ui/button';\nimport type { ReactNode } from 'react';\n\nexport interface FormActionsProps {\n  cancelHref: string;          // where Cancel navigates to\n  submitLabel: ReactNode;      // \"Create Invoice\", \"Edit Invoice\", etc.\n  cancelLabel?: ReactNode;     // default \"Cancel\"\n  pending?: boolean;           // optional: disable submit during action\n}\n\nexport function FormActions({\n  cancelHref,\n  submitLabel,\n  cancelLabel = 'Cancel',\n  pending = false,\n}: FormActionsProps) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n      <Link\n        href={cancelHref}\n        className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n      >\n        {cancelLabel}\n      </Link>\n      <Button type=\"submit\" aria-disabled={pending}>\n        {submitLabel}\n      </Button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Public API\n\n**Props**\n- `cancelHref: string` — Cancel destination (required; the only behavioural difference between forms).\n- `submitLabel: ReactNode` — submit button text/content (required).\n- `cancelLabel?: ReactNode` — defaults to `\"Cancel\"`.\n- `pending?: boolean` — optional pending flag for `useFormStatus` integration.\n\n**Slots** — none needed for the four current call sites; the shape is small and parameterised entirely by props. If a future form needs extra actions (e.g. a \"Save draft\" button), add a single `extras?: ReactNode` slot rendered *before* Submit rather than redesigning the API.\n\n### Call-site diff\n\n```tsx\n// create-form.tsx (replace the 9-line <div>)\n<FormActions cancelHref=\"/dashboard/invoices\" submitLabel=\"Create Invoice\" />\n\n// edit-form.tsx\n<FormActions cancelHref=\"/dashboard/invoices\" submitLabel=\"Edit Invoice\" />\n```\n\n### One caveat worth flagging\n\nThe confidence on this finding is 0.7 (lower than the exact-duplicate findings at 0.95) because two of the four copies live in `final-example` and two in `starter-example` — these may be intentionally independent tutorial snapshots. If that's the case, the extraction should happen *within* each example, giving you two `FormActions` modules (one per app), not one shared across both. Worth confirming before you reach across the example boundary.",
